  "body": "## Finding Description\nThe Covenant core batches operations via [`Covenant.multicall()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-covenant/blob/d5ebe4461564b46cacf8a90cf11add29470ef001/src/Covenant.sol#L507-L524) and enforces ETH payment correctness at the batch level. Per [`ICovenant.multicall()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-covenant/blob/d5ebe4461564b46cacf8a90cf11add29470ef001/src/interfaces/ICovenant.sol#L261), “Does not check msg.value received. Instead, it uses any msgValues encoded in data and sends those onwards,” with a final pre/post balance check.\n\nImplementation uses a global boolean [`Covenant._isMulticall`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-covenant/blob/d5ebe4461564b46cacf8a90cf11add29470ef001/src/Covenant.sol#L516-L518) to skip per-call payment checks inside a batch. The inner logic is:\n\nAffected function code:\n```solidity\nfunction multicall(bytes[] calldata data) external payable returns (bytes[] memory results) {\n    uint256 balanceBeforeCall = address(this).balance - msg.value;\n\n    _isMulticall = true;\n    results = MulticallLib.multicall(data);\n    _isMulticall = false;\n\n    if (address(this).balance != balanceBeforeCall) revert Errors.E_IncorrectPayment();\n    return results;\n}\n\nfunction _checkPayment(uint256 msgValue) private {\n    if (msg.value != msgValue && !_isMulticall) revert Errors.E_IncorrectPayment();\n}\n```\n\nBatch execution uses delegatecall on self:\n\nAffected function code:\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-covenant/blob/d5ebe4461564b46cacf8a90cf11add29470ef001/src/libraries/MultiCall.sol#L26-L32\n```solidity\nlibrary MulticallLib {\n    function multicall(bytes[] calldata data) internal returns (bytes[] memory results) {\n        results = new bytes[](data.length);\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {\n            results[i] = Address.functionDelegateCall(address(this), data[i]);\n        }\n        return results;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nSince nested calls run in the same context, an inner `multicall()` toggles the shared `_isMulticall` flag to `true` and then resets it to `false` before returning to the outer loop. This breaks the intended payment bypass for the remainder of the outer batch, making subsequent operations fail their individual `msg.value == msgValue` check in `_checkPayment()`.\n\nThe `noDelegateCall` guard does not prevent this because it only checks that delegatecall does not change `address(this)`:\n\nAffected function code:\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-covenant/blob/d5ebe4461564b46cacf8a90cf11add29470ef001/src/libraries/NoDelegateCall.sol#L12-L15\n```solidity\nmodifier noDelegateCall() {\n    if (address(this) != originalAddress) revert E_DelegateCallNotAllowed();\n    _;\n}\n```\n\nIn our case, `Address.functionDelegateCall(address(this), ...)` keeps `address(this)` unchanged, so `noDelegateCall` does not revert.\n\nRoot cause:\n- The payment-bypass is controlled by a single global flag `Covenant._isMulticall`.\n- Nested `multicall()` calls toggle this flag back to `false` mid-batch due to shared state and delegatecall, re-enabling per-call payment checks and causing reverts.\n\nHighest impact scenario:\n- A batch that legitimately relies on multicall semantics for per-call `msgValue` forwarding is front-loaded with a nested `multicall()` (even empty). When the inner returns, `_isMulticall == false`, so the next operations hit `_checkPayment()` and revert with `Errors.E_IncorrectPayment`.\n\n## Impact\nMedium.\n\n- Denial-of-service on otherwise valid batched flows, preventing governance/ops batches (e.g., `updateState()`, `mint()`, `swap()`) from executing atomically as designed.\n- No direct asset theft, but material protocol availability impact aligns with Medium per c4 docs\n\n## Likelihood \nHigh.\n\n\n## Recommendation\nMake the multicall payment-bypass nesting-safe by tracking depth (or by save/restoring the old state).",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add the PoC test to `C4PoC.t.sol`\n\n```solidity\n    function test_Multicall_NestedResetsFlag_CausesIncorrectPaymentRevert() public {\n        // Reconstruct market params matching the created market\n        MarketParams memory marketParams = MarketParams({\n            baseToken: _mockBaseAsset,\n            quoteToken: _mockQuoteAsset,\n            curator: _mockOracle,\n            lex: address(lex)\n        });\n\n        // Build two updateState calls with different msgValues and non-empty oracle data\n        bytes memory data1 = hex\"01\";\n        bytes memory data2 = hex\"02\";\n\n        bytes memory callA = abi.encodeWithSelector(\n            covenant.updateState.selector,\n            _marketId,\n            marketParams,\n            data1,\n            uint256(1)\n        );\n\n        bytes memory callB = abi.encodeWithSelector(\n            covenant.updateState.selector,\n            _marketId,\n            marketParams,\n            data2,\n            uint256(2)\n        );\n\n        // 1) Baseline: no nesting → should succeed (per-call payment check skipped in multicall)\n        bytes[] memory batch1 = new bytes[](2);\n        batch1[0] = callA;\n        batch1[1] = callB;\n        covenant.multicall{value: 3}(batch1);\n        // Both oracle updates executed\n        assertEq(MockOracle(_mockOracle).callCount(), 2, \"baseline batch should execute two oracle updates\");\n\n        // Reset tracking\n        MockOracle(_mockOracle).resetTracking();\n\n        // 2) Nested multicall: inner toggles `_isMulticall` back to false → subsequent call reverts\n        bytes[] memory inner = new bytes[](0);\n        bytes memory nested = abi.encodeWithSelector(covenant.multicall.selector, inner);\n\n        bytes[] memory batch2 = new bytes[](3);\n        batch2[0] = nested;\n        batch2[1] = callA; // will trigger _checkPayment with msg.value=3 vs msgValue=1 when _isMulticall == false\n        batch2[2] = callB;\n\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.E_IncorrectPayment.selector);\n        covenant.multicall{value: 3}(batch2);\n    }\n```\n\nRun:\n```bash\nforge test --mt test_Multicall_NestedResetsFlag_CausesIncorrectPaymentRevert\n```\n\n- Baseline: Two `updateState()` calls with `msgValue` 1 and 2, non-empty `data`, executed via `multicall{value:3}` succeed; `MockOracle.callCount() == 2`.\n- Nested: Prepend an inner `multicall()` call, then the same two `updateState()` calls, execute `multicall{value:3}`. This reverts with `Errors.E_IncorrectPayment` because `_isMulticall` is reset to `false` mid-batch.",
